WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.023
Use a five-layer lookup method.

2
00:00:02.023 --> 00:00:05.024
Start with RISC-V International for standards.

3
00:00:05.024 --> 00:00:07.438
Use Eclipse documents for governance.

4
00:00:07.438 --> 00:00:13.767
Use the OpenHW charter, committees, and programme material for collaboration scope and direction.

5
00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.943
Use project manuals and repositories for implementation choices.

6
00:00:17.943 --> 00:00:21.009
Use tests, CI, tags, and releases for evidence.

7
00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:24.206
If a sentence mixes layers, split it into claims.

8
00:00:24.206 --> 00:00:31.775
Next, choose CVA6 or CVE2 and trace one feature from specification to manual, RTL, verification, and pinned release.

